WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.020
- [Josh] In July,

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.330
a story began to circulate
of a top secret meeting

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.130
between Taiwan and the US.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.540
A newspaper had published a summary

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.700
from a secret meeting
in the South China Sea.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.533
At the meeting,

00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:11.910
US officials had reportedly
asked Taiwan to research

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.880
and develop biological weapons
in a high security laboratory

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.550
at the National Defense
Medical Center in Taipei.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.190
The report began to spread
across local media in Taiwan.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.320
- The US State Department
has denied a report

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.210
saying that the US asked Taiwan

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.010
to develop biological weapons.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.780
- Develop bioweapons.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.330
- The only problem? None of it was true.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.200
It's part of what analysts

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.460
and Taiwanese government officials say

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.563
was a Chinese disinformation campaign.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.200
Ahead of Taiwan's presidential elections,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.720
there's been a striking increase
in disinformation attacks

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.010
targeting the island,

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.650
which the government and
analysts attribute to China.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.210
Taiwan's government says Beijing

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.740
wants to influence the elections

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.890
because whomever next occupies
the Presidential Palace here

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.770
is going to dictate Taiwan's
relationship with China.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.830
- We have seen the
Chinese cognitive warfare

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.050
and disinformation campaign.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.170
And I think they have sharpened
their tools in this regard.

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:04.560
- Every day we have
hundreds of battlefields

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.620
about misleading
information on social media.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.550
- [Josh] China's Communist government

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.080
has never ruled Taiwan,

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.300
but it claims it is part of its territory.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.060
In recent years, China has
stepped up military exercises

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.560
around the self-ruled
island of 24 million people.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.580
Now, Taiwan is going to the polls

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.440
to vote for its next President.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:23.760
The two main parties are the ruling

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.260
Democratic Progressive Party,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.910
which has forged tighter ties with the US

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.650
under President Tsai Ing-wen.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.120
And the opposition Kuomintang,

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.490
which favors friendlier
relations with China.

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:33.323
Leading up to the vote,

00:01:33.323 --> 00:01:34.650
the Taiwanese government has seen a wave

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.469
of disinformation pointing to Beijing,

00:01:36.469 --> 00:01:38.580
with many of the attacks
designed to cast doubt

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.650
on the island's relationship with the US.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.450
Taiwan's Foreign Minister
says these attacks

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.640
are part of an effort to influence voters.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.270
- It will all be different
kinds of scenarios

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.249
portrayed by the Chinese side.

00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:52.230
For example, they continue to say

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.940
that the choice in this election

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.040
is in between war and peace,

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:00.150
and if you vote for the DPP's
candidate, it will mean war.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.850
- What are you seeing this year
compared to previous years?

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.490
Is it worse, better, different?

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:07.260
And how concerned are you about it?

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.377
- The Chinese always try to play its role.

00:02:10.377 --> 00:02:13.380
And they try to influence
the outcome of the election,

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:14.550
one way or another.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:15.750
In the previous times,

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:19.440
they went through military
threat against Taiwan,

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.392
and this time around,

00:02:20.392 --> 00:02:22.800
we noticed that China has been gearing up

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:26.160
its cognitive warfare and
disinformation campaign

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.033
against Taiwan.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.070
- [Josh] As the vote nears,

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.510
researchers are working to identify

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.940
and counter disinformation
targeting the election.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.200
- They are trying to manipulate

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:39.090
the Taiwanese people's opinion
against the ruling party.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.700
- [Josh] Ethan Tu is the
founder of Taiwan AI Labs,

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.650
an NGO that uses artificial intelligence

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.230
to trawl through social
media to identify trends

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.420
and instances of misleading information.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.238
- Taiwan is number one in terms

00:02:50.238 --> 00:02:53.318
of the foreign government's
false information

00:02:53.318 --> 00:02:55.290
11 years in a row.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:59.160
So in Taiwan, overall, every day,

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.820
every individual has received some kind

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.990
of information manipulation.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.190
- [Josh] Taiwan receives thousands

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.750
of disinformation attacks every day

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.420
that mirror Chinese
state media narratives.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:10.800
In the two months leading up to the vote,

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.380
attacks peaked at more than 15,000 a day.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:18.210
- We believe that there's
consistent funding support

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:22.950
to manipulate the democratic
country's election in Taiwan.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.020
And the reason of that is Taiwan's

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:29.973
at a very unique position
between United States and China.

00:03:29.973 --> 00:03:31.890
- Beijing has threatened action against

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:34.650
any perceived moves by Taiwan
to assert independence.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.210
China is trying to influence the election

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.090
because it doesn't want this
man, William Lai, to win.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:42.180
Beijing sees Lai as an advocate
for Taiwanese independence

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.280
and it worries that Taiwan
will move further away

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.050
if he becomes President.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.330
Lai is currently serving
as Taiwan's Vice-President,

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.100
and has said he would
maintain the status quo

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.045
in relations with China
established by President Tsai.

00:03:53.045 --> 00:03:56.045
(speaking Mandarin)

00:04:03.273 --> 00:04:06.273
(speaking Mandarin)

00:04:13.589 --> 00:04:16.672
(speaking Mandarin)

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.700
- [Josh] The surge in
disinformation comes amid efforts

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.250
by Beijing to ramp up military
and diplomatic pressure

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:27.300
on Taiwan.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.370
But China has denied that
it's trying to interfere

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:30.810
in the upcoming election.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:32.250
Beijing's Taiwan Affairs Office

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.020
said accusations of Chinese interference

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.160
in the election are false

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:38.100
and that it respects the
island's current social system.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.720
Chinese leaders Xi Jinping has vowed

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.790
to eventually take control of the island,

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.410
making Taiwan's status a flashpoint

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:46.050
in relations between the US and China.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.820
Whoever wins this election
will set the course

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.060
of Taipei's relationship with
Beijing at a critical moment.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.560
(tense music)

